import html,json
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1] / 'samples'
spec=json.loads((root/'synthetic_cases.json').read_text())
real=json.loads((root/'real_sources.json').read_text())
md=['# Official real CT files for research testing','', 'Source: [KiTS23](https://github.com/neheller/kits23), Nicholas Heller and the KiTS23 contributors. Images are hosted in the Hugging Face repository linked by the official downloader.','', '**Data terms:** CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. The maintainers require contact for commercial purposes; see the [source terms](https://github.com/neheller/kits23#license-and-attribution).','', '| Case | CT download | Reference mask | Compressed CT size |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
realrows=[]
for case in real['cases']:
 ident=case['id']; im=case['image']; mask=case['mask']; size=im['bytes']/1048576
 md.append(f"| {ident} | [CT .nii.gz]({im['url']}) | [Mask .nii.gz]({mask['url']}) | {size:.1f} MiB |")
 realrows.append(f'<tr><th scope="row">{ident}</th><td><a href="{im["url"]}">Download real CT</a><br><small>{size:.1f} MiB · .nii.gz</small></td><td><a href="{mask["url"]}">Reference mask</a><br><small>{mask["bytes"]/1024:.0f} KiB · .nii.gz</small></td></tr>')
md += ['', 'Save each image and its mask in a separate case folder. Select the CT image as input; use the mask only as a reference overlay. The labels are 0 background, 1 kidney, 2 tumor, 3 cyst.', '', 'Both original pairs were downloaded, hashed and consumed by the native engine on 28 September 2026. Case 00002 was used for training and case 00003 for held-out patch validation in a tiny engineering probe. These are demonstration files, not an independent clinical test set. Native file compatibility does not establish model accuracy.', '', 'The images use FLOAT64 storage. Decompression and float-tensor conversion require substantially more memory than the download size; use a desktop for these full scans. The public ParsecScope page currently confirms local file selection only; server-side masking is not enabled.', '', 'Pinned revisions and SHA-256 hashes are in real_sources.json. Downloads remain at the original publishers.']
(root/'REAL_CT_DOWNLOADS.md').write_text('\n'.join(md)+'\n')
cards=[]
for c in spec['cases']:
 cards.append(f'''<article class="card"><div class="tag">SYNTHETIC · NO PATIENT DATA</div><h3>{html.escape(c['title'])}</h3><img src="previews/{c['id']}.png" alt="{html.escape(c['title'])}: CT-like phantom and known reference overlay" width="920" height="483"><div class="links"><a href="{c['image']}" download>Download image</a><a href="{c['reference_mask']}" download>Reference mask</a></div><p class="small">96 × 96 × 64 voxels · {c['spacing_mm'][0]} × {c['spacing_mm'][1]} × {c['spacing_mm'][2]} mm spacing</p></article>''')
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Download ParsecScope synthetic NIfTI examples and official real CT research files."><title>ParsecScope · Client test images</title><style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#173348;--muted:#536c7c;--line:#d9e5ed;--brand:#086c8e}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#f4f8fb;color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,sans-serif}header{background:white;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}header div,main,footer{max-width:1080px;margin:auto;padding:22px 26px}header div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}a{color:var(--brand);text-underline-offset:3px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,5vw,52px);line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:18px 0}h2{font-size:27px;margin:38px 0 12px}h3{font-size:20px;margin:8px 0 15px}p{max-width:860px}.lead{font-size:19px;color:var(--muted)}.notice{background:#fff7e6;border:1px solid #ead6ae;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px}.button{display:inline-block;background:var(--brand);color:white;border-radius:9px;padding:12px 18px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;margin:12px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;padding:22px}.card img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:920px;margin:auto;border-radius:10px}.tag{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:750;color:#587184}.links{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:16px}.small,small{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white}th,td{text-align:left;padding:15px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{font-weight:650}.legend{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:12px 0 25px}.dot{display:inline-block;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:3px;margin-right:7px}footer{font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}@media(min-width:900px){.card{padding:24px 34px}}@media(max-width:500px){header div,main,footer{padding:18px}td,th{padding:10px}.links{gap:14px}}
</style></head><body><header><div><strong>ParsecScope</strong><a href="https://parsecscope-coder.github.io/parsecscope-client/">Open client preview</a></div></header><main><div class="tag">CLIENT TEST FILES · 28 SEPTEMBER 2026</div><h1>Try a scan.<br>Know what to expect.</h1><p class="lead">Three small synthetic volumes with known masks, plus official real CT downloads for research testing.</p><div class="notice"><strong>Available today:</strong> download the files, inspect the example previews, and test local file selection. The public client page does not yet upload scans or generate AI masks. The reference overlays below are supplied labels, not model predictions.</div><a class="button" href="https://parsecscope-coder.github.io/parsecscope-client/samples/ParsecScope_Client_Test_Images_v1.zip" download>Download synthetic test pack</a><p class="small">ZIP includes all three examples, masks, previews, instructions and links to the real scans. Unzip it first. For image input, choose a file from the images folder.</p><h2>Synthetic examples</h2><p>Mathematical CT-like phantoms for checking file handling and geometry. They are deliberately simplified and cannot establish real-patient accuracy.</p><div class="legend"><span><i class="dot" style="background:#36d4b1"></i>Kidney shapes</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#ffaf54"></i>Tumor shape</span><span><i class="dot" style="background:#85aaff"></i>Cyst shape</span></div>'''+''.join(cards)+'''<h2>Real CT research files</h2><p>These KiTS23 scans and matching reference masks were successfully loaded by our native engine on 28 September. Download from the original publishers using the links below.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Input scan</th><th>Known labels</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(realrows)+'''</tbody></table></div><p class="small">Credit: Nicholas Heller and the KiTS23 contributors. <a href="https://github.com/neheller/kits23#license-and-attribution">KiTS23 data terms: CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. The maintainers require contact for commercial purposes. Case 00002 was used for training and case 00003 for held-out patch validation in our small engineering probe; these downloads are not an independent clinical test set.</p><p class="small">The full scans expand considerably in memory. Use a desktop, retain the .nii.gz extension and keep each scan beside its matching mask in a separate case folder.</p><h2>Inspect locally</h2><p><a class="button" href="viewer.html">Open local NIfTI slice viewer</a></p><p>Select a synthetic CT image and its matching reference mask. The viewer processes files in your browser and does not upload them or run AI inference. Full real scans may exceed its 128 MiB expanded-size limit.</p><h2>What to check</h2><ol><li>Download an image and choose it on the client preview page. Confirm the filename, size and format recognition.</li><li>In a NIfTI viewer or enabled test backend, load the matching mask as an overlay. Check alignment and label colors.</li><li>Report the case ID, browser or viewer, expected result and any error message.</li></ol><p><a href="README.md">Full instructions</a> · <a href="synthetic_cases.json">Synthetic geometry and counts</a> · <a href="real_sources.json">Real-file sources and hashes</a> · <a href="validation.json">Native loader checks</a></p></main><footer>Research and software testing only. Not for diagnosis or treatment. No patient data is embedded in the synthetic pack.</footer></body></html>'''
(root/'index.html').write_text(page)
print('Sample gallery and real CT download guide created')
